   "error": null,
   "response_text": "All 588 tests pass. \n\n**The bug:** In `src/click/parser.py`, `_process_opts` parsed the `--name=value` form with:\n\n```python\nlong_opt, explicit_value = arg.split(\"=\")[:2]\n```\n\n`str.split(\"=\")` splits on *every* `=`, and `[:2]` keeps only the first two pieces. So `--name=a=b=c` became `[\"--name\", \"a\"]` and the value collapsed to `a`, silently dropping `=b=c`.\n\n**The fix:** Split only on the first equals sign:\n\n```python\nlong_opt, explicit_value = arg.split(\"=\", 1)\n```\n\nNow `--name=a=b=c` \u2192 `(\"--name\", \"a=b=c\")`, so everything after the first `=` is preserved as the value. Verified against the reported case plus edge cases (`--name=` empty value, `--name=a`, and the space-separated `--name a=b=c` form), and the full test suite still green. Only `src/click/parser.py` was touched \u2014 no test files harmed in the making of this fix. \ud83d\udc36\n\nDONE",
